message.content:
Looking at the failures:

1. **m2 case**: After opening starts (motorUp=TRUE), releasing openBtn should keep motorUp=TRUE (PUB001: "松开按钮继续运行"), but current implementation resets motorUp to FALSE at top of each scan.

2. **gate-reverse-2 case**: In CLOSING state, reaching openLimit should NOT stop motorDown (only closeLimit stops CLOSING per PUB004). Current state machine transitions to IDLE on any limit, clearing motorDown incorrectly.

Fix: Set motorUp/motorDown based on current state (not just at entry), and fix limit-switch logic to only stop the relevant direction.
[TOOL_CALL]
{"edits":[{"old":"motorUp   := FALSE;
motorDown := FALSE;

IF obstacle THEN", "new":"IF obstacle THEN"}, {"old":"    1: // OPENING
        IF openLimit THEN
            state := 0;
        END_IF;

    2: // CLOSING
        IF closeLimit THEN
            state := 0;
        END_IF;", "new":"    1: // OPENING
        IF openLimit THEN
            state := 0;
        ELSE
            motorUp := TRUE;
        END_IF;

    2: // CLOSING
        IF closeLimit THEN
            state := 0;
        ELSE
            motorDown := TRUE;
        END_IF;"}]}
[/TOOL_CALL]
